.TH KICAD-IMPORTER 1 "2026-08-28" "kicad-importer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kicad-importer \- import component ZIP files into KiCad project libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kicad-importer
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kicad-importer init
.RB [ \-\-library
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-downloads
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B kicad-importer import
.RI [ FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.RB [ \-\-interactive ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kicad-importer
imports downloaded electronic component ZIP archives (SnapMagic/SnapEDA,
ComponentSearchEngine/SamacSys, Ultra Librarian and similar services) into a
KiCad project library from the command line.
It drives the same import pipeline as the KiCad Component Importer desktop
application: symbols are merged into the project symbol library, footprints
and 3D models are copied into organized library folders, symbols are linked
to their footprints, 3D model paths are repaired using
.B ${KIPRJMOD}
so the project stays portable, and the libraries are registered in the
project's
.I sym-lib-table
and
.IR fp-lib-table .
A copy of each imported ZIP is kept in the project's
.I source_zips
folder and every import is validated.
.PP
The tool can be run from the project root or any of its subfolders: it walks
up the directory tree until it finds the
.I .kicad-importer
configuration file and treats that folder as the project root.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
Create or update the
.I .kicad-importer
configuration file.
When no configuration exists yet, it is created in the nearest ancestor
directory (including the current directory) containing a
.I *.kicad_pro
file.
The command is re-runnable: only the flags passed on the current invocation
are changed, other settings are kept.
The first run requires
.BR \-\-library .
.TP
.BI \-\-library " NAME"
Name of the project library that components are imported into.
The importer creates
.IB libraries/ NAME .kicad_sym
and
.IB libraries/ NAME .pretty
under the project root and registers them in the project library tables.
.TP
.BI \-\-downloads " PATH"
Optional downloads folder that
.B import
searches in addition to the current directory.
A leading
.B ~
is expanded and the path is stored absolute.
A warning is printed if the folder does not exist.
.SS import
Import one or more component ZIP archives into the configured project
library.
Requires a discovered
.I .kicad-importer
file with a configured library.
.PP
If a part is already present in the library, the import stops before touching
any files and prompts
.RB \(lq "Overwrite? [y/N]" \(rq .
The message reports whether the library's copy was modified since it was
imported (the Symbol, the Footprint, or both), and treats missing or unreadable
import metadata as modified.
Answering
.B y
overwrites the symbol, footprint and 3D model from the ZIP; any other answer
cancels that part, leaving it unchanged.
A cancelled part still counts as a success and, with
.BR \-\-delete ,
its ZIP is kept.
When standard input is not a terminal and
.B \-\-yes
is absent, the prompt is answered
.RB \(lq no \(rq
without blocking.
.TP
.I FILE
ZIP file to import, given as a path or a bare filename.
A bare filename is looked for first in the current directory, then in the
configured downloads folder.
When the argument is omitted, all ZIP files from both locations are
aggregated and presented in a fuzzy picker:
.BR fzf (1)
when installed, otherwise a built-in numbered picker that filters by
substring.
Cancelling the picker exits without importing.
.TP
.BR \-\-all ", " \-a
Import every eligible ZIP in the current directory.
A first pass inspects each archive and skips files that contain no KiCad
symbol library or footprint assets.
Each candidate is then imported with a per-file OK or FAILED line and a
final summary.
Cannot be combined with a
.I FILE
argument.
.TP
.BR \-\-delete ", " \-d
Delete each ZIP after it was imported successfully.
A part whose overwrite was cancelled keeps its ZIP, but this is not a failure
and does not stop the other imported ZIPs from being deleted.
With
.BR \-\-all ,
the delete phase is skipped entirely when any import failed.
.TP
.BR \-\-interactive ", " \-i
Open a terminal editor for each imported symbol to reconstruct its pin layout
before it is written to the library.
The symbol is drawn as an ASCII chip; pin names on the top and bottom sides are
drawn vertically.
Arrow keys move the cursor between pins;
.B Space
selects a pin so the arrow keys move it (reordering within a side, carrying it
around a corner onto the neighbouring side, or jumping it to the opposite side
when the arrow points into the body).
.B S
inserts a blank spacer slot and
.B d
deletes one;
real pins are never deleted.
Pressing
.B y
twice accepts and regenerates the symbol with an auto-sized body on the
2.54 mm grid; pressing
.B Esc
then
.B Enter
cancels and imports the symbol exactly as merged.
With
.BR \-\-all ,
the editor runs once per imported ZIP in turn.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Overwrite existing parts without prompting.
Answers every overwrite prompt with
.RB \(lq yes \(rq,
which is the usual choice for non-interactive and scripted use.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print full Python tracebacks for unexpected errors instead of one-line
messages.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored per project in
.IR .kicad-importer ,
a small INI file in the project root:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[kicad-importer]
library = MyBoard_Parts
downloads = /home/you/Downloads
.fi
.RE
.PP
The file can be edited by hand or updated by re-running
.BR "kicad-importer init" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .kicad-importer
Per-project configuration file, located in the KiCad project root.
.TP
.I libraries/
Created under the project root; holds the symbol library, the
.I .pretty
footprint library, 3D models, source ZIP copies, metadata and backups.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a cancelled picker and parts whose overwrite was cancelled.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: file not found, missing configuration, or at least one
import failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, or no command given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure a project once, from anywhere inside it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kicad-importer init --library MyBoard_Parts --downloads ~/Downloads
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a specific downloaded archive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kicad-importer import ul_TPS631000DRLR.zip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pick an archive interactively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kicad-importer import
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import every component ZIP in the current folder and clean up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kicad-importer import --all --delete
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1)
.PP
Full documentation and the desktop application:
.UR https://github.com/robertxdx/component-importer-for-kicad
